# Design Patent Specification: Ergonomic Point-of-Care Automated Health Diagnostic Kiosk

### 1. Abstract & Scope of the Claim
The ornamental and ergonomic structural design for an **Automated Health Diagnostic and Emergency Triage Kiosk**, characterized by a cantilevered non-contact vital sensing alcove, an integrated bio-isolated electrode hand-rest, and a secure multi-bin pharmaceutical dispenser chassis, as illustrated in the accompanying CAD boundary diagrams.

---

### 2. Physical Architecture & Dimensional Envelope
* **External Chassis Dimensions:** $1950\text{ mm}$ (Height) $\times 820\text{ mm}$ (Width) $\times 740\text{ mm}$ (Depth).
* **Ergonomic Accessibility:** Complies with ADA Wheelchair Reach Range guidelines ($380\text{ mm}$ to $1220\text{ mm}$ interactive HMI zone).
* **Material Selection:** Antimicrobial powder-coated CRCA steel ($1.6\text{ mm}$ gauge) with high-impact polycarbonate optical shields.

